  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday Night through Wednesday) \nIssued at 1225 AM CST Thu Nov 12 2026\n\nRain chances start to increase from the west Saturday evening and \novernight, continuing through the day Sunday, though there remain \nsignificant synoptic uncertainties in the path and timing of the \nupper wave. Most ensemble members track the central precipitation \naxis somewhere between I-40 and well south of the Red River (through \ncentral Texas), though there are a few outliers on either side. \nRainfall amounts of 1 to 3 inches appear likely along that axis \n(but, again, this could be southwest of our forecast area). A few \nembedded thunderstorms may be possible, but instability may be a \nlimiting factor.\n\nUncertainty in the temperature forecast peaks on Sunday, largely due \nto the aforementioned synoptic / precipitation uncertainties. A few \nrepresentative interquartile ranges are copied below:\n\n - Ponca City / Woodward / Oklahoma City: 45 to 55\n - Durant: 52 to 59\n - Lawton / Hobart: 49 to 62\n - Wichita Falls: 52 to 70\n\nHigher confidence in the forecast for Monday and Tuesday once the \nwave passes where we should see highs in the 50s to lower 60s with \nsome cloudiness (but no rain). From there we transition into more \nsouthwesterly flow and the potential for active weather that brings.\n\nDay",
